---
title: Diffusion-limited aggregation
---
Particles are fired at a small open seed, and each digs the last solid tile it crossed before it reached open floor [[t:103-108 s:13]].

## The rule
```text
dig a small seed at the center of a solid map
while less than a share of the map is open:
    start a particle on a random tile
    move it until it stands on open floor:
        a random step at a time (walk), or straight at the center (attractor)
    dig the last solid tile it stood on, and with symmetry its mirror image
```

The talk shows three versions that differ in how a particle travels: a simple one, a central attractor, and the attractor with a symmetry [[t:103-104 t:111-112 t:115-116]]. The demo of the simple version moves its particle one random step at a time [[c05:55-80]].

## Step through it
@@steps limit=5 mid=2

## Controls
@@control mode
How a particle travels. `walk` steps at random, `attractor` follows a line to the center, and `symmetric` does that and digs each tile’s mirror image too [[c05:55-80 c06:56-68 c07:56-77]].
@@control floor_divisor
Particles keep coming until one over this number of the map’s tiles is open: a third, in all three demos [[c05:43 c06:43 c07:43 g]].

## What it produces, measured
@@measured

The talk calls the simple version’s map very winding, and guaranteed to be contiguous [[t:109]]. The walking version is both: {{c05.regions.max}} region on every seed, and {{c05.dead_ends.median}} dead ends at the median against cellular automata’s {{c03.dead_ends.median}} [[run:c05.regions.max c05.dead_ends.median c03.dead_ends.median]]. The attractor and the symmetric version are not contiguous: {{c06.regions.median}} and {{c07.regions.median}} regions at the median, and never fewer than {{c06.regions.min}} and {{c07.regions.min}} [[run:c06.regions.median c07.regions.median c06.regions.min c07.regions.min]]. Their particles follow a Bresenham line to the center [[c06:56-60]]. Such a line can step diagonally, so a dug tile can touch the cave only at a corner, and walking is four-way [[own]].

## Where it fails
@@fails

The simple version’s walk has no cap in the talk’s code [[c05:55-80]]. Ours has one, which {{c05.fails.guard-hit}} of these seeds reach [[run:c05.fails.guard-hit]].

## What it combines with
@@combines

The talk also fires particles at a finished map, which is [erosion](#dla-erode) [[t:191-193]].

